Kept a Volto session signed in at the authorization endpoint when the browser also sends a `Basic` `Authorization` header. A browser resends cached basic credentials to every path on a host, so signing in to a page behind a proxy's basic auth made every later sign-in to a relying party loop back to the login page. Only a `Bearer` header, the one plone.restapi reads, now takes precedence over the session cookie, and basic credentials for a real Plone user still win. @ericof
